From df28c6e26f256b23201749e75070978b9890f2c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 20:14:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Fix dead row-tap on mobile in the unified activity panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The detail pane is hidden md:flex — a real flex sibling that narrows
the list, which has no sensible mobile shape, same call already made
for right-utility-panel.tsx. Below md that left a row tap doing nothing
visible: setSelectedId fired but the panel it would have opened never
renders. Row actions (approve/reject/dismiss/cancel) were unaffected
since those buttons live in the row itself, not the hidden panel.

Now checks viewport width on tap: desktop opens the inline detail pane
as before, mobile navigates to the item's full page instead — the same
fallback right-utility-rail.tsx already uses for its own panels on
mobile, rather than a silent no-op.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Lv1Fc4mc6LHrFpMHiHajTt
